# Ozma multi-seat supervisor
# Install as /etc/ozma/ozma-multiseat.env for ozma-multiseat.service, or as
# ~/.local/etc/ozma/ozma-multiseat.env for a systemd --user unit.
# EnvironmentFile syntax: KEY=VALUE, no shell expansion; values are not
# shell-quoted.

# The supervisor enumerates this X display. It must be reachable from the
# unit's account. A system unit cannot read a logged-in user's Xauthority under
# $HOME (ProtectHome=yes), so either prefer a user unit or point XAUTHORITY at
# a readable host path (for example /etc/ozma/Xauthority).
DISPLAY=:0
# XAUTHORITY=/etc/ozma/Xauthority

# The unit passes --seats-file <state>/seats.json; the running supervisor
# loads/reuses it and updates it atomically. --print-plan/--dry-run never write
# it and are never used by the unit.

# Optional extra flags. Ownership, routing, audio, private X servers, and input
# isolation apply host resources and are opt-in; enable only what this host is
# provisioned for. Use one OZMA_MULTISEAT_ARGS line (systemd splits it at
# whitespace, so do not quote individual values).
# OZMA_MULTISEAT_ARGS=--apply-ownership --apply-routing --audio-router pipewire
# OZMA_MULTISEAT_ARGS=--seat-display xvfb --seat-display-size 1280x800
# OZMA_MULTISEAT_ARGS=--status-port 7391 --restart-backoff-max-ms 30000
# OZMA_MULTISEAT_ARGS=--input-isolation helper --input-helper /usr/lib/ozma/ozma-seat-input

RUST_LOG=ozma_multiseat=info,ozma_node=info
